[74.409019, "o", "\u001b[35m_\u001b[0m\u001b[35minternal.cli.main import main\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[35mModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pip'\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[35m```\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[35mThis is a classic half-deleted install: something removed the package tree but left `dist-info` behind. That leftover metadata is also why the obvious fix fails — `ensurepip` checks the metadata first:\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[35m```\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[35m$ python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade --default-pip\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[74.409085, "o", "\u001b[35mRequirement already satisfied: pip in .../site-packages (24.3.1)   ← lies\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[35m```\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[35m## The fix\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[35m1. Moved the orphaned metadata out of the way (backed up to `/tmp/pip-24.3.1.dist-info.bak`):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[35m   ```bash\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[35m   mv /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info /tmp/pip-24.3.1.dist-info.bak\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[35m   \u001b[0m\u001b[35m```\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[37m2. Re-ran \u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[32mensurepip\u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[37m, which then installed cleanly from its bundled wheel:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[74.410649, "o", "\u001b[37m   \u001b[0m\u001b[37m```\u001b[0m\u001b[38;5;9mbash\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[74.412197, "o", "\u001b[37m   \u001b[0m\u001b[37mpython3\u001b[0m\u001b[37m -\u001b[0m\u001b[37mm\u001b[0m\u001b[37m ensurepip\u001b[0m\u001b[37m --\u001b[0m\u001b[37mupgrade\u001b[0m\u001b[37m --\u001b[0m\u001b[37mdefault-pip\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[37m   \u001b[0m\u001b[38;5;8m#\u001b[0m\u001b[38;5;8m Successfully installed pip-24.3.1\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[37m   \u001b[0m\u001b[37m```\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[34m##\u001b[0m\u001b[37m \u001b[0m\u001b[34mVerification\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[74.412277, "o", "\u001b[37m|\u001b[0m\u001b[37m Check \u001b[0m\u001b[37m|\u001b[0m\u001b[37m Result \u001b[0m\u001b[37m|\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[74.412946, "o", "\u001b[37m|\u001b[0m\u001b[37m---\u001b[0m\u001b[37m|\u001b[0m\u001b[37m---\u001b[0m\u001b[37m|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[37m|\u001b[0m\u001b[37m \u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[32mpython3 -m pip --version\u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[37m \u001b[0m\u001b[37m|\u001b[0m\u001b[37m \u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[32mpip 24.3.1 ... (python 3.13)\u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[37m \u001b[0m\u001b[37m|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[37m|\u001b[0m\u001b[37m \u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[32mpip --version\u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[37m / \u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[32mpip3 --version\u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[37m \u001b[0m\u001b[37m|\u001b[0m\u001b[37m OK \u001b[0m\u001b[37m|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[37m|\u001b[0m\u001b[37m \u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[32mpip check\u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[37m \u001b[0m\u001b[37m|\u001b[0m\u001b[37m No broken requirements found \u001b[0m\u001b[37m|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[37m|\u001b[0m\u001b[37m Wheel install (\u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[32msix\u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[37m) \u001b[0m\u001b[37m|\u001b[0m\u001b[37m ✅ installed, then removed \u001b[0m\u001b[37m|\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[74.41299, "o", "\u001b[37m|\u001b[0m\u001b[37m \u001b[0m\u001b[1;33m**\u001b[0m\u001b[1;33mSource build\u001b[0m\u001b[1;33m**\u001b[0m\u001b[37m (\u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[32m--no-binary :all: charset-normalizer\u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[37m) \u001b[0m\u001b[37m|\u001b[0m\u001b[37m ✅ built + installed, then removed \u001b[0m\u001b[37m|\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[74.413022, "o", "\u001b[37m|\u001b[0m\u001b[37m Dependency resolution (\u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[32mrequests\u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[37m dry-run) \u001b[0m\u001b[37m|\u001b[0m\u001b[37m ✅ resolves all 5 deps \u001b[0m\u001b[37m|\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[74.413029, "o", "\r\n"]
[74.413227, "o", "\u001b[37mI uninstalled the test packages afterwards, so site-packages is back to just \u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[32mpip\u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[37m.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[34m##\u001b[0m\u001b[37m \u001b[0m\u001b[34mTwo things worth knowing\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[74.417994, "o", "\u001b[37m-\u001b[0m\u001b[37m \u001b[0m\u001b[1;33m**\u001b[0m\u001b[1;32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[1;32m/usr/bin/python3\u001b[0m\u001b[1;32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[1;33m (Python 3.11) has no pip either.\u001b[0m\u001b[1;33m**\u001b[0m\u001b[37m That's Debian's own interpreter, separate from your \u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[32m/usr/local/bin/python3\u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[37m (3.13.1) that owns \u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[32mpip\u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[37m/\u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[32mpip3\u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[37m. It was already that way and isn't what was broken. If you need it, use \u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[32mapt install python3-pip\u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[37m rather than touching \u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[32m/usr/local\u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[37m.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[37m-\u001b[0m\u001b[37m \u001b[0m\u001b[1;33m**\u001b[0m\u001b[1;32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[1;32msetuptools\u001b[0m\u001b[1;32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[1;33m isn't installed\u001b[0m\u001b[1;33m**\u001b[0m\u001b[37m — that's normal for Python 3.13, whose \u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[32mensurepip\u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[37m no longer bundles it. Modern pip uses build isolation and fetches build backends on demand, which the source-build test above confirmed. Only install it if you use legacy tooling that does its own \u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[32msetup.py\u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0"]
[74.418134, "o", "m\u001b[37m imports.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[37mTo avoid recurrence, prefer virtualenvs (\u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[32mpython3 -m venv .venv\u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[37m) rather than installing into site-packages directly — a stray \u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[32mrm -rf\u001b[0m\u001b[32m`\u001b[0m\u001b[37m can't break your interpreter that way.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[74.469077, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@90ba06d7c50e:/app# "]
[79.900688, "i", "\u0004"]
[79.90091, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\r\nexit\r\n"]
